What is printed based on Java's pass-by-value behavior?

```java
public class Main {
    public static void modify(int x) {
        x = 50;
    }
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int a = 10;
        modify(a);
        System.out.println(a);
    }
}
```

What is the output of the following recursive method call `factorial(4)`?

```java
public static int factorial(int num) {
    if (num == 0) return 1;
    return num * factorial(num - 1);
}
```

What is printed by the recursive countdown method call `countdown(3)`?

```java
public static void countdown(int num) {
    if (num <= 0) {
        System.out.print("End");
    } else {
        System.out.print(num + " ");
        countdown(num - 1);
    }
}
```

What is the output of the recursive decimal-to-binary method `decToBin(13)`?

```java
public static void decToBin(int num) {
    if (num == 0) {
        System.out.print(0);
    } else if (num > 0) {
        decToBin(num / 2);
        System.out.print(num % 2);
    }
}
```
